   "reproduction": "unreproduced: no reproduction is needed. The lease reply does send the request unredacted. The question is whether that adds any exposure, and that can only be judged by tracing where gate commands come from.",
   "evidence": "server/workers.ts:66 sends `{ ...request, cwd: \"\" }`. The gate config comes only from repository content. engine.ts:~486-506 builds gates with `detectGates(dir)` / `detectGates(wt.path)` and `readRetryFiles(repoConfig)`, where repoConfig = `readFileAt(wt.path, trustedSha, \".limitless.toml\")`. detect.ts reads only `.limitless.toml` or package.json detection. The bundle route builds `git bundle create` from refs pointing at headSha and baseSha with no negative refs, so it ships the full reachable history, including the files that contain these commands. A credential written literally into a gate command is therefore already committed and already sent to the worker, which the owner approved for this repository. The reviewer only got this to happen by registering a synthetic credential and writing it into a command."
  }
