  "id": "F2",
  "title": "One attempt can stay leased forever while its requests retry",
  "file": "src/workers/client.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Suppose the bundle download keeps failing at the transport level, for example because the coordinator takes longer than the listener's 60-second idle timeout to build a large bundle. The worker then retries forever while its heartbeats keep renewing the lease. The job never moves to another worker or to local execution, so the run's gates hang indefinitely.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: this needs a long-lived loopback worker with an injected 503 or transport fault and an advanced clock. The evidence below is quoted code.",
   "evidence": "client.ts:137-159 `call` loops `for (;;)` with no attempt limit or deadline, retrying any transport error (`.catch(() => undefined)`) or status >= 500 after `sleep(delay)`. The job stays `reported: true` until run()'s finally, so `heldJobs()` keeps listing it in heartbeats. db/workers.ts:175 heartbeat() then sets `lease_expires_at = now + lease` for every held job it receives. sweep() fails a leased job only on revoke, lease expiry or a stale heartbeat, never on overall elapsed time. The listener sets `idleTimeout: 60` while bundle creation allows `timeoutMs: 300_000`, so a slow bundle build is a plausible repeating transport failure. lan.ts attach polls until the job is done or failed, so it waits forever."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A worker keeps heartbeating while bundle downloads continually fail. Its gate job remains pending indefinitely instead of moving to another worker and eventually running locally.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-570.ts\"",
    "output": "F2 {\"elapsedCoordinatorSeconds\":8020,\"bundle503s\":10,\"state\":\"leased\",\"attempt\":1,\"leaseStillFuture\":true}"
   },
   "evidence": "The probe ran the actual worker loop, injected persistent bundle 503 responses and advanced coordinator time by 20 seconds per held-job heartbeat. Heartbeats used the actual listener handler through an in-process transport because loopback listening was unavailable. HEAD retries with `for (;;)`, bounding only each individual request and retry delay. Heartbeat renewal writes `this.now() + this.times.lease`; sweep checks freshness and lease expiry but has no attempt deadline. Consequently successful heartbeats perpetually prevent failover. Base retried idle heartbeats but had neither job downloads nor renewable gate leases."
  }
 },
